{"title":"2015 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An arithmetic sequence is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained by adding a constant to the previous term. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f333ff33137ccf8bd0bb24d0cc92bb40428344d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,5,8,11,14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> is an arithmetic sequence with five terms, in which the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the constant added is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Each row and each column in this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbf62794748fc97d1bfe454296f10da375126bac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> array is an arithmetic sequence with five terms. The square in the center is labelled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> as shown. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2a56a58f7cc3f5d0f4adce873e6ecb5d1038b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }21\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }31\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }36\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }40\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e463abe580eaf777a86e44ccfbdd1acb90f714.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(3.85cm); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,(2.5,2.1),N); for (int i=0; i&lt;=5; ++i) draw((i,0)--(i,5), linewidth(.5));  for (int j=0; j&lt;=5; ++j) draw((0,j)--(5,j), linewidth(.5)); void draw_num(pair ll_corner, int num)  { label(string(num), ll_corner + (0.5, 0.5), p = fontsize(19pt)); }  draw_num((0,0), 17); draw_num((4, 0), 81);  draw_num((0, 4), 1);  draw_num((4,4), 25);   void foo(int x, int y, string n) { label(n, (x+0.5,y+0.5), p = fontsize(19pt)); }  foo(2, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 3, &quot; &quot;);   [/asy]\" width=\"185\" height=\"185\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We begin filling in the table.  The top row has a first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a fifth term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so we have the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/5321e9674c70d760b6c63198b599cda8a3edd37f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25-1}4=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />.  This means we can fill in the first row of the table:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c028f3edd8159a97e7b756a43ead831d4eb02ad3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(3.85cm); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,(2.5,2.1),N); for (int i=0; i&lt;=5; ++i) draw((i,0)--(i,5), linewidth(.5));  for (int j=0; j&lt;=5; ++j) draw((0,j)--(5,j), linewidth(.5)); void draw_num(pair ll_corner, int num)  { label(string(num), ll_corner + (0.5, 0.5), p = fontsize(19pt)); }  draw_num((0,0), 17); draw_num((4, 0), 81); draw_num((1,4), 7); draw_num((2,4), 13); draw_num((3,4), 19); draw_num((0, 4), 1);  draw_num((4,4), 25);   void foo(int x, int y, string n) { label(n, (x+0.5,y+0.5), p = fontsize(19pt)); }  foo(2, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 3, &quot; &quot;);   [/asy]\" width=\"185\" height=\"185\" />\n</p><p>The fifth row has a first term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and a fifth term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, so the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1fc57693d23feb31e5b549707330a31f035ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81-17}4=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" />.  We can fill in the fifth row of the table as shown:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/540608620fbcae9b59ab2dc17ec5eab91393e103.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(3.85cm); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,(2.5,2.1),N); for (int i=0; i&lt;=5; ++i) draw((i,0)--(i,5), linewidth(.5));  for (int j=0; j&lt;=5; ++j) draw((0,j)--(5,j), linewidth(.5)); void draw_num(pair ll_corner, int num)  { label(string(num), ll_corner + (0.5, 0.5), p = fontsize(19pt)); }  draw_num((0,0), 17); draw_num((4, 0), 81); draw_num((1,4), 7); draw_num((2,4), 13); draw_num((3,4), 19); draw_num((4, 4), 25); draw_num((0, 4), 1); draw_num((1, 0), 33); draw_num((2, 0), 49); draw_num((3, 0), 65);    void foo(int x, int y, string n) { label(n, (x+0.5,y+0.5), p = fontsize(19pt)); }  foo(2, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(2, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 1, &quot; &quot;); foo(0, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 0, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(1, 4, &quot; &quot;); foo(3, 3, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 2, &quot; &quot;); foo(4, 3, &quot; &quot;);   [/asy]\" width=\"185\" height=\"185\" />\n</p><p>We must find the third term of the arithmetic sequence with a first term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and a fifth term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.  The common difference of this sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09edf76e62ad8e939f32b11760b1a8e477ab60b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{49-13}4=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"38\" />, so  the third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f0fe04a4cfe52041a31db008cfaca5e1a8a09e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13+2\\cdot 9=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"160\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The middle term of the first row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf3d1c7c18d4d19f3628148ff1d7b9d34bf9990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25+1}{2}=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" />, since the middle number is just the average in an arithmetic sequence. Similarly, the middle of the bottom row is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d55f5d94c5db79e80503013666a701eee2173cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17+81}{2}=49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />. Applying this again for the middle column, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b5137f4b7fafe6492b6f682121bd9d7ce40d301e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{49+13}{2}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is simply the average of the average values of both diagonals that contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3cabca85d5d71e8ad21af959cba1cf117de946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1+81}{2}+\\frac{17+25}{2}}{2} =\\frac{\\frac{82}{2}+\\frac{42}{2}}{2} = \\frac{41+21}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"360\" height=\"40\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1BUbtuK_MXI\">https://youtu.be/1BUbtuK_MXI</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/tKsYSBdeVuw?t=1258\">https://youtu.be/tKsYSBdeVuw?t=1258</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QFC4VmFa9Kc\">https://youtu.be/QFC4VmFa9Kc</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 8\">2015 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /